---
import SiteLayout from '../../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const href = (value: string) => `${base.replace(/\/?$/, '/')}${value.replace(/^\/+/, '')}`;
const flow = 'Sandbox platform\n' +
  '├── ConnectionAgent Domain  ·  Agent / Runtime / Skills\n' +
  '├── Tool Plane              ·  discovery / gateway / common capabilities\n' +
  '├── Environment Plane       ·  environment substrate / simulated & real worlds / env-fabric\n' +
  '├── Evaluation              ·  Benchmark assets / evaluation engine\n' +
  '├── Control / Surface       ·  experiment control / console\n' +
  '└── Shared Foundation       ·  nodus\n' +
  '\nPlatform-level composition and compatibility governance.\n' +
  'Each component retains its own contract and fact authority.';
---
<SiteLayout title="Sandbox Platform Architecture" lang="en" description="Sandbox platform layers, reading paths, and technical documentation authority boundaries.">
  <section class="home-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Sandbox / Architecture</span>
    <h1>Sandbox platform architecture</h1>
    <p>Sandbox composes Agent, tool, environment, experiment-control, and evaluation components into repeatable systems. This page is the platform-level map and reading guide; component responsibilities, technical flows, and current status belong to owner-maintained documentation and acceptance evidence.</p>
    <div class="home-actions">
      <a href={href('/en/components/sandbox/#platform-architecture-en')}>Detailed architecture and responsibility boundaries <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/runbooks/real-5gc/')}>Real 5GC runbook <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/interfaces/real-5gc-evidence/')}>Interfaces and evidence <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      <a href={href('/en/benchmark/')}>Benchmark evaluation framework <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Platform layers</h2>
    <p>The diagram shows the target responsibility taxonomy. It is not a claim that every migration or end-to-end acceptance step is complete.</p>
    <pre><code>{flow}</code></pre>
    <p>Physical repository names may differ from target names. The relevant owner repository defines each component's implementation, contract, and authoritative facts; platform documentation explains how components work together.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>Choose a reading path</h2>
    <div class="reading-list">
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/components/sandbox/#platform-architecture-en')}>
        <span class="reading-number">01</span>
        <span><strong>How do components work together, and who owns each fact?</strong><small>Owner-maintained platform architecture, component responsibilities, authority boundaries, and the R1 / R2-B real 5GC flows.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/runbooks/real-5gc/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">02</span>
        <span><strong>How do I run and validate a real 5GC?</strong><small>Step-by-step checks for topology, sessions, PFCP, user-plane connectivity, and supporting evidence.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/interfaces/real-5gc-evidence/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">03</span>
        <span><strong>Which interfaces and evidence establish the result?</strong><small>Request/response contracts, fact sources, evidence correlation, and independent judgment boundaries.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
      <a class="reading-item" href={href('/en/benchmark/')}>
        <span class="reading-number">04</span>
        <span><strong>How is Agent reliability evaluated?</strong><small>Start with the platform-level evaluation map, then read the owner docs for assets, execution lifecycle, and judgment.</small></span>
        <span class="reading-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="home-section">
    <h2>How to read status</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Target architecture</strong> describes intended responsibilities and composition, not completed delivery.</li>
      <li><strong>Owner implementation</strong> is defined by versioned documentation, code, and contracts in the component's repository.</li>
      <li><strong>Acceptance status</strong> depends on the relevant tests and evidence; documentation sync, code merge, or a successful static-site build does not establish end-to-end acceptance.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>For technical details and the current R1 / R2-B status, read the <a href={href('/en/components/sandbox/#platform-architecture-en')}>owner architecture document</a> and the <a href={href('/en/runbooks/real-5gc/')}>runbook</a>. Do not infer delivery status from target names.</p>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
